"The numbering arts are strong where they touch the ground and blind where they turn abstract."
"An Aiestan taking Nala's graph of a function would call it a pretty puzzle and no more."
"To Hallick the same drawing would be a grammar of change, which is what he has chased for years."
"The Army would take a general aiming method at once, and take the inventor along with it."
"Arcana has done the Empire's work so long that no one has tried an engine of heat and pressure."
"A working non-arcane engine would be worth more to the war effort than any sequence."
"The curve is the real find: a method of drawing rules is a method for every table in the Empire."
"Hallick can price the lens rule; he has no idea yet what to call the thing that produced it."
"Any table the Empire keeps, from aims to Spire upkeep, is a candidate for the same treatment."
"The Academy would name her a founder over the drawing of a single curve, if it ever heard of her."
